course: dictionary
lesson: 1429
title: Meat-eaters and meat-eating plants
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Carnivorous means eating meat, mostly other animals. «Carnivorous» is an adjective, so it describes something: a carnivorous animal. Lions, sharks and eagles are carnivorous.
explain: Carnivorous can also describe a plant. A carnivorous plant catches and digests insects or small animals, like the Venus flytrap or the sundew. The animals that eat meat are called carnivores.
explain: Read the sentences around a word for clues. «There are more than 600 kinds of carnivorous plants, and all of them still make their food from sunlight.» Even though these plants catch insects, they still use light, air and water to make food, just like other plants. «No plant can eat a person», so a cartoon showing a plant swallowing someone is not true.
fact: Carnivorous means eating meat, mostly other animals.
fact: A carnivore is an animal that eats meat. A herbivore eats only plants, and an omnivore eats both.
fact: Carnivorous plants usually grow in poor, boggy soil, so they get extra nutrients from insects.
fact: «There are more than 600 kinds of carnivorous plants.»
fact: All carnivorous plants still make their food from sunlight.
exercise: What does carnivorous mean? | Eats plants only | Lives only in water | *Eats meat, mostly other animals | Grows very tall
exercise: Which word is the noun for an animal that eats meat? | plant | herbivore | *carnivore | sunlight
exercise: Where do carnivorous plants get extra nutrients from? | From the sun only | From the soil alone | From other plants | *From insects
test: Which animal is carnivorous? | Horse | *Shark | Rabbit | Cow
test: Is this true? «A carnivorous plant can eat a person.» | *No, plants make their food from light, air and water | Yes, but only in cartoons | Only very large plants can do it | Yes, carnivorous plants swallow people
exam: Which sentence uses carnivorous correctly? | *Lions are carnivorous animals that eat meat | A carnivorous plant can eat a whole cow | The carnivorous rain fell all day | The carnivorous lettuce grows in the garden
